{
  "_comment": [
    "CANONICAL cross-repo parity fixtures for ReviewSeed's query assembly.",
    "",
    "These cases are run against BOTH implementations of the shared query-building logic:",
    "  - MCP app: server/query.ts, imported directly (tests/unit/parity.test.ts)",
    "  - Website: index.html's page-global buildBooleanQuery/buildFrameworkQuery,",
    "    called via Playwright page.evaluate (~/code/pubmedseed/tests/verify-parity.mjs)",
    "",
    "The two implementations have DIFFERENT function signatures (the website's are",
    "positional and predate the MCP app's object-based ones). Each runner adapts the",
    "canonical `pool` shape below to its own call convention — what must match is the",
    "OUTPUT STRING, not the calling code.",
    "",
    "This file is the single source of truth. The website reads it from the MCP app",
    "repo (path via REVIEWSEED_MCP_APP env var); it is deliberately NOT duplicated,",
    "because a stale copy would silently pass and defeat the entire purpose.",
    "",
    "When you fix or change shared query-assembly behavior, add a case here FIRST,",
    "then make both repos pass it.",
    "",
    "`idClauseCases` cover idClause/restrictToIds — the per-source 'restrict to these",
    "records' clause that recall validation is built on. Each form was verified against",
    "the live API on 2026-07-30 with a negative control. A wrong clause here doesn't",
    "error; it reports 0% recall, which reads as a catastrophically broken search."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "boolean": [
    {
      "name": "keyword + mesh, pubmed",
      "target": "pubmed",
      "pool": {
        "keywords": [
          "gabapentin"
        ],
        "mesh": [
          "Neuralgia"
        ],
        "eric": [],
        "queries": [],
        "ericQueries": [],
        "ctQueries": []
      },
      "kwFields": {},
      "opts": {},
      "expected": "\"gabapentin\"[tiab] AND \"Neuralgia\"[MeSH Terms]"
    },
    {
      "name": "multiple keywords are OR'd and grouped",
      "target": "pubmed",
      "pool": {
